self-driving cars are already here  widespread adoption of this technology  will lead to a traffic less pollution  and fewer car accidents these cars bring  to light a long-standing hypothetical  dilemma how moral should we make our  robots what if an autonomous vehicle is  faced with a choice to either kill its  passenger or kill others how should it  be programmed in online surveys  participants approve of autonomous  vehicles that sacrifice the driver to  save many others basically a utilitarian  approach that aims to preserve the most  amount of life but respondents would  prefer not to buy these kinds of cars  and they don't want regulations that  require self-sacrificing algorithms in  fact such regulations would make them  less willing to buy a self-driving car  the rise of autonomous vehicles creates  a social dilemma roads would be much  safer if there are more autonomous cars  but programming that would actually make  driving safer might prevent people from  buying these vehicles imagine shopping  for a car and having a choice a car that  sacrifices a driver on occasion or a  preserved passenger at all costs car  what would you do
 

